{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qmxwzzn5zqq2aktbusexfqkrnopicm4cjwwjhfbieho5sw4sbuqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Final state:\n\n## Result: `ALL CONFIGURATIONS VERIFIED` (47 checks × 4 build configurations)\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (`translation/`): `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (25 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (25 rows), plus `VERIFICATION.md` and `ci/verify_all.sh`.\n\n**Phase D symbol parity:** the C `.so` exports 12 symbols; the Rust `.so` exports all 12 with identical names and no extras. `ldd -r` is clean on both. Nothing was stubbed and no C source was untranslated — `src/lib.c` is the only translation unit and all of it was present. This is enforced by `tests/phase_d_symbols.rs`, not just checked by hand.\n\n**Phases B & C:** 25/25 + 25/25 rows pass, all through `libloading` against both `.so` files (the Rust crate is never linked directly). Highlights: exhaustive 256-value `char` domain, the full 6561-combination `mathop` corner cross-product, byte-exact `printf` comparison via `dup2`, full 240-byte history-buffer comparison including padding, and fork-isolated crash comparison for NULL pointers.\n\n### The one real divergence found — fixed\nWith `history == NULL`, C died with **SIGSEGV** but the Rust `.so` died with **SIGABRT** (`null pointer dereference occurred`). The translated logic was correct; rustc's UB checks (enabled with debug assertions) instrument raw-pointer dereferences and turned the C's unchecked NULL load into a panic. Fixed in `Cargo.toml` (`[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false`), so the dev artifact matches the release artifact and the C. `src/lib.rs` needed **no logic changes** — wrapping arithmetic, C's truncating `%`, the `default:` enum fallback, the count-reset-on-NULL branch and the silent drop at capacity were all already faithful.\n\n### One disclosed non-match\n`divide_operation(INT_MIN, -1, _)` / `modulo_operation(INT_MIN, -1, _)` is C undefined behaviour: `idiv` traps and the process dies with SIGFPE, so C produces no value to match. Rust returns `INT_MIN`/`0`. `ub_divide_int_min_by_minus_one` pins both observed outcomes in forked children and asserts every adjacent input still matches exactly; `mathop_would_trap()` excludes these inputs from randomized batches.\n\n### Two test-harness bugs I found and fixed\nWorth flagging because both would have produced false confidence: libtest writes its own `test <name> ... ok` progress lines to fd 1, which landed *inside* a captured stdout region of a concurrent test (moved all stdout comparisons into a `harness = false` sequential binary, and the parser now rejects foreign lines); and a comparison helper dereferenced a not-yet-allocated buffer, segfaulting the test process instead of reporting a mismatch.\n\n`cargo test` works from a completely clean tree (verified after `rm -rf target ../c_src/build`) — the harness bootstraps both the C library and the cdylib, since `cargo test` alone does not emit the cdylib. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified; only `build/` was regenerated."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":804,"cache_read_input_tokens":185431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":804,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8e3c062-943d-43a8-a3d0-1f35c227133a","uuid":"28801975-31b0-45e7-a319-9fdc61a2486c","timestamp":"2026-08-28T03:22:40.081Z"}
